1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:15,000
DeltaProof: private AI scope review for software agencies.
Captured walkthrough using synthetic example data.

2
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:40,000
A client asks for spreadsheet exports and team invitations.
The reviewer traces the request against the agreed scope.

3
00:00:40,000 --> 00:01:15,000
Local MiniLM retrieves exact clauses. Conflicting evidence stays visible.
A reviewer proposes 12 hours for export and 20 hours for team access.

4
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:45,000
The proposal contains 32 extra hours and USD 2,880 at USD 90 per hour.
Parallel dependencies produce one workday of delay after buffer.

5
00:01:45,000 --> 00:02:10,000
Deferring invitations removes 20 hours and USD 1,800.
The export path still determines the delivery delay.

6
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:35,000
Remove the team-account exclusion from retrieved evidence.
The recommendation changes to insufficient evidence.

7
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:55,000
Export the internal review packet with sources and assumptions.
No client message or approval happens automatically.

8
00:02:55,000 --> 00:03:10,000
22 tests pass. The real-model smoke check matches 10 of 12 cases.
This small synthetic evaluation is not a contract-accuracy benchmark.
